Mara Ellis, guarded_practical voice (constructed harness arc)

[joined]
9 July 1993
Joined Jonah. Still not sure about this.

For now, this is better than being on my own.

[scratch -> wound.scratch_shrug]
11 July 1993
Scratch on the left hand. Not worth the ink.

Writing it down anyway, which probably says something.

[player bandage -> care_player.guarded]
13 July 1993
Bandage from Jonah. On the left hand.

Don't much like being the one who needs something.

[escape -> escape.guarded]
15 July 1993
Close one. We both got clear.

That's the part worth writing down.

[trust callback -> trust.guarded]
17 July 1993
Earlier I wrote, 'For now, this is better than being on my own.'

I meant it then. I want to stay now, and not just because the other options are worse.

[loss -> loss.guarded]
19 July 1993
Ruth is dead.

Don't know what to put after that.

[bite -> bite.watchful]
21 July 1993
The bite is on my right hand.

I keep checking it, like checking will change something. It's the one thing on my list that isn't going to get better.

[quarantine -> crisis_self.quarantine]
23 July 1993
They want me kept apart for now. It's the sensible thing.

I would have decided the same. I'd just rather not have been the one it was about.

[late fever -> symptoms.late_bite_guarded]
24 July 1993
Hard to write.

Jonah, if you read this: it wasn't your fault. It was a bite.

--- one passage per new scene, per voice ---
[witnessed_hurt / blunt_brave] Ruth got knocked about a bit. / I would like to say I didn't laugh at the noise Ruth made. I would like to say that.
[witnessed_hurt / warm_candid] Ruth got hurt and I couldn't get there fast enough. / I hope it looked worse than it was.
[conflict / blunt_brave] Had it out with Ruth. I said what I'd been holding in. / Feels better. Feels worse. Both.
[conflict / warm_candid] Had it out with Ruth. I said what I'd been holding in. / Feels better. Feels worse. Both.
[breakdown / blunt_brave] Shouted at the air for a while. / The air took it well. I didn't.
[breakdown / warm_candid] Lost my temper at nothing in particular. / Nothing in particular had it coming.
[joy / blunt_brave] Felt good today. Actually good. / For once I believed we'd be all right, and nobody had to talk me into it.
[joy / warm_candid] Felt good today. Actually good. / For once I believed we'd be all right, and nobody had to talk me into it.
[promise_broken / blunt_brave] The supply run we talked about never happened. / I know things come up. I also know what was said.
[promise_broken / warm_candid] Supply run: still waiting. / I've started keeping score, and I don't like that I have.
[talk / blunt_brave] Pep talk from Jonah. It worked, which is annoying.
[talk / warm_candid] Jonah said the right thing at the right time. / Suspicious. Grateful. Mostly grateful.
[study / blunt_brave] Found a dead Santa. Spent a while looking at him. / I'm not going to recover from that emotionally.
[study / warm_candid] Studied a corpse, like a lunatic. Learned nothing. / Will probably do it again.
[respects / blunt_brave] Paid my respects to a stranger. / I hope someone does that for me. Actually, I hope nobody has to.
[respects / warm_candid] Stopped to give one of the dead a moment. It seemed like someone should.
[workout / blunt_brave] Worked out. For a few minutes it felt like an ordinary life with extra zombies.
[workout / warm_candid] Exercised. Cardio is a survival skill now. / I used to say that as a joke.
[reading / blunt_brave] Read some of 'hunting knife'. / Nobody in it had to check the doors twice. I liked that.
[reading / warm_candid] Did some reading. Better than thinking.
[washed / blunt_brave] Washed the dirt off. / It felt like putting something down that I'd been carrying.
[washed / warm_candid] Washed the dirt off. / It felt like putting something down that I'd been carrying.
[repair / blunt_brave] Looked after the hunting knife. / Things that are looked after last longer. People too.
[repair / warm_candid] Patched up the hunting knife. It'll hold. / Most things do, if you ask nicely.
[fight_story / blunt_brave] 5 of them at the gas station. / If anyone asks, it was more.
[fight_story / warm_candid] Did most of it with a baseball bat. / I've started thinking of it as a friend. That's probably a bad sign.
[tale_told / blunt_brave] Told the old story again. It was 5, not 9. / It isn't really about the number anymore.
[tale_told / warm_candid] Told the story again. It was 5. It's 9 now. / It'll be more by winter.
[place / blunt_brave] Walked into a police station like we owned it. / I suppose we do now.
[place / warm_candid] Walked into a police station like we owned it. / I suppose we do now.
[work / blunt_brave] Sawing all day, or what felt like it. / We're building something. Nice to be building something.
[work / warm_candid] Sawing all day, or what felt like it. / We're building something. Nice to be building something.
[burial / blunt_brave] Grave work. / The dead don't complain. That's more than I can say for my back.
[burial / warm_candid] Buried 6 strangers. / Somebody has to. Today it was me.
[mercy / blunt_brave] I did it. Ruth won't come back. / That was the point. That's what I keep telling myself.
[mercy / warm_candid] Ruth was bitten, and it was decided. I was the one who did it. / I don't want to write anything else.
[milestone / blunt_brave] 8 days. Still breathing. Still here.
[milestone / warm_candid] A week with Jonah, give or take. / Longer than I gave it.
[quiet / blunt_brave] Nothing to report. That's the best kind of entry.
[quiet / warm_candid] Nothing to report. That's the best kind of entry.
[quiet page written by the controller] 26 July 1993 / Summer. It used to mean something else.
